Complexity: O(n log n) with binary search (bisect) per element, pops amortized O(n). Since stack list is sorted, bisect works. n up to 1e5, fine.

Implementation:

```python
from bisect import bisect_left

class Solution:
    def shadowPairs(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:
        stack = []  # non-decreasing
        ans = 0
        for x in nums:
            while stack and stack[-1] > x:
                stack.pop()
            ans += bisect_left(stack, x)
            stack.append(x)
        return ans
```

